🕵️‍♂️ Digital Forensics & OSINT: Image Metadata Analysis

This project demonstrates a digital forensics and open-source intelligence (OSINT) investigation using ExifTool and Yandex Reverse Image Search. The objective was to extract actionable intelligence from two image files provided as part of a forensic challenge.

🛠️ Tools Used

ExifTool – for extracting image metadata
Yandex Reverse Image Search – for identifying visual matches
Online Maps & Coordinate Tools – for interpreting and validating GPS data
🔍 Investigation Process

1. Metadata Extraction with ExifTool
I examined the first image using exiftool, revealing key data:

Camera Model: Canon EOS 550D
Timestamp: 2021:11:02 13:20:23
User Comment: "relying on altered metadata to catch me?"
GPS Coordinates: 32°40'3.87" S, 279°29'31.87" W
2. Analyzing Metadata Clues
The GPS coordinates fell outside valid ranges (longitude > 180°), indicating spoofed data.
However, the timestamp and camera details were valid and relevant.
3. Reverse Image Search (Yandex)
The second image lacked GPS metadata, so I used Yandex Reverse Image Search:

Uploaded the image to Yandex.
Analyzed visual matches (architecture, landscape, context).
Multiple matches pointed to Kathmandu, Nepal.


